{"author":{"id":"40e3ba2788b3b9fc163c354afc44e5f9d225bcf0a27e679aaa878dd6135c6dcb"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1781351098,"nonce":"dkjHZkRD2eIFZDPTQpDBE6vRVSo=","title":"Decompressor/cdir parser hardening against adversarial (truncated) input","message":"A memory-io prefix-sweep fuzzer (feed every truncated prefix of a valid archive to uc2_open -\u003e read_cdir -\u003e finish_cdir -\u003e extract) surfaced robustness gaps in the libunuc2-heritage parser on damaged input. Fixed in the f049d6d commit (deterministic, verified): (1) decompress_block match-length overflow -- a short bits_get could underflow len and overrun the 64KB cb.data window; the NDEBUG-disabled assert is now a runtime UC2_Damaged check; (2) decompress_cdir bounded cdir_range.end to the actual decompressed byte count instead of the allocation, so a damaged cdir that passes the 16-bit checksum by chance is not parsed into uninitialised heap; (3) CLI handle/FILE leak on the cdir-error path.\n\nREMAINING (this issue): the fuzzer still finds a RARE, heap-state-dependent OOB in the cdir-skip/tag path (uc2_finish_cdir -\u003e uc2_read_cdir(0) -\u003e uc2_get_tag, decompress.c:858) on archives whose cdir REGION is truncated (e.g. a 21KB rANS-cdir archive cut at ~360-500 bytes). It reproduces ~1 in 60+ runs (uninitialised-heap-dependent), only under ASan -- a plain Release build reads mapped heap and does not fault, so it is not a CI crash but it is a real latent bug. Root cause not fully pinned: likely a wild cdir_range or a state-machine corner in start_read / the cdir offset handling on a malformed XHEAD, producing a stale/garbage pointer the skip-walk dereferences.\n\nNEXT: (a) systematic bounds + state-machine validation across the cdir parser (start_read, decompress_cdir, uc2_read_cdir, uc2_get_tag) treating ALL header/offset/size fields as adversarial; (b) a STABLE libFuzzer or AFL++ harness (the throwaway prefix-sweeper is the prototype: mem-io serving the first N bytes, then the full open/read/finish/extract flow with a discard writer) added as a non-CI fuzz target plus a corpus of minimised crashers; (c) once deterministic, a truncation regression test can be added to the suite. Found while implementing f049d6d.","files":null}]}